eir dietary needs. This dish features boiled vegetables accompanied by a creamy pea sauce, emphasizing soft and easily digestible ingredients. The recipe is part of a broader effort to provide safe and enjoyable food options for those with swallowing difficulties, highlighting the importance of tailored nutrition in clinical settings. The relationship between this dish and the 'Manual de Disfagia Orofaríngea' underscores its relevance in dietary management for dysphagia patients [Data: Entities (1450); Relationships (1274)].\n\n## The critical role of salt in nutrition\n\nSalt, while essential for health, poses significant risks when consumed in excess. It is a primary source of sodium in diets and is crucial for flavoring and preserving food. However, high salt intake is linked to various health issues, including cardiovascular mortality and cancer. The World Health Organization (WHO) provides guidelines on salt consumption to mitigate these risks, emphasizing the need for careful monitoring of sodium intake. This dual nature of salt as both a necessary nutrient and a potential health hazard is a central theme in nutritional discussions [Data: Entities (1482); Relationships (5929, 6544, 6543)].\n\n## Controlled sodium diet for health management\n\nThe 'Dieta Controlada en Sodio' is a dietary regimen designed to restrict sodium intake, particularly for individuals with hypertension or renal issues. This diet is crucial for managing fluid balance and blood pressure, helping to prevent complications associated with excessive sodium consumption. The relationship between this controlled diet and various health conditions, such as chronic renal failure and hypertension, highlights its importance in clinical nutrition and patient care [Data: Entities (11350); Relationships (9166, 13118)].\n\n## Link between salt consumption and cardiovascular mortality\n\nThere is a significant association between high salt consumption and increased cardiovascular mortality rates. Studies